invariant: INV-42
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: proof/prove-one.sh rsa_sign64_crt
reason: rsa_sign64_key_ok compares all but the top limb of p * q with the
  modulus, so a key whose primes multiply to a value that differs from
  the modulus in that limb alone is admitted, and the arithmetic then
  runs over primes the test did not hold to the modulus. One changed bit
  of a prime moves the product's low limbs too, so the faulted keys
  bin/rsa_sign_test_host makes are still refused. The rsa_sign64_crt
  harness states the test over every limb the product has.

--- old
    for (size_t i = 0; i < 2 * limbs; i++) {
        differ |= product[i] ^ n[i];
    }
--- new
    for (size_t i = 0; i + 1 < 2 * limbs; i++) {
        differ |= product[i] ^ n[i];
    }
